    {
      "type": "panel",
      "key": "zelf_schrijven",
      "title": "Write a process variable",
      "label": "Schrijven",
      "input": false,
      "tableView": false,
      "collapsible": false,
      "components": [
        {
          "type": "content",
          "key": "schrijven_uitleg",
          "input": false,
          "tableView": false,
          "html": "<h4>Writing one, and watching it arrive</h4><p>The field below is a <code>ZAC_TYPE</code> of <code>ZAC_process_data</code>: a plain input whose <code>key</code> is the name of a process variable. Type something into it and read it back in the two cells underneath, which show the same key from each of the two objects. Both are empty until the value gets there.</p><ol><li><strong>Save.</strong> The whole submission is stored as one task variable. Reopen the task and the left cell fills in; the right one is still empty.</li><li><strong>Complete.</strong> Now every submitted key is written into the process variables, so the right cell fills in too and the value stays there for the rest of the process.</li></ol><p>That is the whole storage model, and it is not specific to <code>ZAC_process_data</code>: <em>any</em> input in the form is stored under its own <code>key</code> the same way. The attribute only marks the field as an input whose key is meant to be a variable name. Which is also the trap &mdash; key a field <code>zaakGroep</code> and completing the task overwrites that process variable. Prefix the keys of your own fields, as this one does.</p>"
        },
        {
          "label": "A process variable of your own",
          "type": "textfield",
          "key": "PD_proefVariabele",
          "input": true,
          "tableView": false,
          "description": "ZAC_TYPE: ZAC_process_data — stored under the key \"PD_proefVariabele\", which is why it is prefixed",
          "attributes": {
            "ZAC_TYPE": "ZAC_process_data"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "key": "terugleesbaar",
          "input": false,
          "tableView": false,
          "numRows": 1,
          "numCols": 2,
          "header": [
            "Stored on the task",
            "Stored on the process"
          ],
          "caption": "",
